<article id="post-8163" class="clearfix post-8163 page type-page status-publish hentry">
			<header class="entry-header">
			<h1 class="entry-title">2026-27 Academic Calendar</h1>		</header><!-- .entry-header -->
	
	<div class="entry-content">
        <div id="pl-8163"  class="panel-layout" ><div id="pg-8163-0"  class="panel-grid panel-no-style" ><div id="pgc-8163-0-0"  class="panel-grid-cell" ><div id="panel-8163-0-0-0" class="so-panel widget widget_black-studio-tinymce widget_black_studio_tinymce panel-first-child panel-last-child" data-index="0" ><h3 class="widget-title"><div class='uc-accordion'>Summer 2026 Graduate Degree Deadlines</div></h3><div class="textwidget"><p><span data-teams="true">Please see the <a href="https://summersession.uconn.edu/dates-fees/">UConn Summer Session website</a> for Summer session dates and deadlines, including the last day to add or drop a course, the last day to withdraw from a course, and grading deadlines.</span></p>
<table id="summer-table" class="table table-bordered">
<thead>
<tr>
<th class="calendar-table" id="date">Date</th>
<th id="deadline-event">Deadline/Event</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Thu, June 11</td>
<td>Deadline to apply for graduation and to submit final Plan of Study (Undergraduate, Master’s, Sixth-Year, and Graduate Certificate students only) for conferral of a Summer 2026 degree.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Mon, Aug 10</td>
<td>Last day for Master’s and Doctoral degree candidates to upload final Master's thesis or Doctoral dissertation to the university-supported repository and submit related paperwork to Degree Audit (<a href="mailto:degreeaudit@uconn.edu">degreeaudit@uconn.edu</a>) for conferral of a Summer 2026 degree.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Mon, Aug 24</td>
<td>Conferral date for Summer 2026 degrees. Final examinations for Plan B Master’s and Sixth-Year Certificate students must be completed by this date.</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Fri, Sep 4</td>
<td>Last day for Degree Audit (<a href="mailto:degreeaudit@uconn.edu">degreeaudit@uconn.edu</a>) to receive the approved Plan B and Sixth-Year Certificate Master’s Report on the Final Exam.</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<p><em> </em></p>
</div></div></div></div><div id="pg-8163-1"  class="panel-grid panel-no-style" ><div id="pgc-8163-1-0"  class="panel-grid-cell" ><div id="panel-8163-1-0-0" class="so-panel widget widget_black-studio-tinymce widget_black_studio_tinymce panel-first-child panel-last-child" data-index="1" ><div class="textwidget"><p class="none">The calendars below are for the current academic year. Links to past, future, and printable calendars are on the sidebar to the right (or at the bottom of this page on mobile devices). Click the buttons below to jump to a particular term.</p>
<ul class="list-inline" style="text-align: center;">
<li><a href="#fall" class="btn btn-warning" role="button">Fall</a></li>
<li><a href="#spring" class="btn btn-success" role="button">Spring</a></li>
<li><a href="#summer" class="btn btn-info" role="button">Summer</a></li>
</ul>
<h3>Fall 2026</h3>
<table id="fall-table" class="table table-bordered" style="width: 100%; height: 888px;">
<thead>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<th class="calendar-table" id="date" style="height: 24px;">Date</th>
<th id="deadline-event" style="height: 24px;">Deadline/Event</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Mon, Aug 31</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Fall semester begins</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Mon, Sep 7</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Labor Day – No classes</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Tue, Sep 8</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Last day to file petitions for course credit by examination (Undergraduate students only)</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Mon, Sep 14</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Tenth day of classes. Courses dropped after this date will have a “W” for withdrawal recorded on the academic record. Last day to add or drop courses without additional signatures (see <a title="Adding or Dropping Courses | Academic Regulations" href="https://catalog.uconn.edu/undergraduate/academic-regulations#registration">Adding and Dropping Courses</a>).</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Mon, Sep 21</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Last day for students to make up Incomplete or Absence grades (continuing Undergraduate students only)</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 72px;">
<td style="height: 72px;">Tue, Sep 22-Mon, Sep 28</td>
<td style="height: 72px;">Examinations for course credit by examination (Undergraduate students only)</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Fri, Sep 25</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Deadline to apply for graduation and to submit Final Plan of Study (Undergraduate, Master’s, Sixth-Year, and Graduate Certificate students only) for conferral of a Fall 2026 degree</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Tue, Sep 29</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Dean’s signature required to add courses</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Mon, Oct 5-Fri, Oct 23</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Mid-semester Grading Period</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Mon, Oct 26</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Registration for the Winter 2027 and Spring 2027 semester via Student Administration System begins</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td rowspan="2" style="height: 48px;">Mon, Nov 16</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Last day to withdraw from a course</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Last day to place courses on or remove from Pass/Fail grading</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 72px;">
<td style="height: 72px;">Sun, Nov 22-Sun, Nov 29</td>
<td style="height: 72px;">Thanksgiving Recess</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 72px;">
<td style="height: 72px;">Fri, Dec 4</td>
<td style="height: 72px;">Last day for Master's and Doctoral degree candidates to upload final Master's thesis or Doctoral dissertation to the university-supported repository and submit related paperwork to Degree Audit (<a href="mailto:degreeaudit@uconn.edu">degreeaudit@uconn.edu</a>) for conferral of a Fall 2026 degree.</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Fri, Dec 11</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Last day of fall semester classes</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Sat, Dec 12-Sun, Dec 13</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Reading Days</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Mon, Dec 14</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Final examinations begin</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Thu, Dec 17</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Reading Day</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Sun, Dec 20</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Final examinations end</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Sun, Dec 20</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Conferral date for Fall 2026 degrees. Final examinations for Plan B Master’s and Sixth-Year Certificate students must be completed by this date.</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 48px;">
<td style="height: 48px;">Wed, Dec 23</td>
<td style="height: 48px;">Semester grades due at 4 pm</td>
</tr>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<td style="height: 24px;">Mon, Jan 4</td>
<td style="height: 24px;">Last day for Degree Audit (<a href="mailto:degreeaudit@uconn.edu">degreeaudit@uconn.edu</a>) to receive the approved Plan B Master’s and Sixth-Year Certificate Report on the Final Exam form. (Graduate students only)</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3 id="spring">Spring 2027</h3>
<table id="spring-table" class="table table-bordered" style="width: 100%; height: 840px;">
<thead>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
<th class="calendar-table" id="date" style="height: 24px;">Date</th>
<th id="deadline-event" style="height: 24px;">Deadline/Event</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr style="height: 24px;">
